the dune saga which is set approximately  20,000 years in our future revolves  around the evolution of mankind both  physically and mentally over the course  of several thousands of years book 1  introduces the character Paul Atreides  the result of a breeding program which  had been going on for many generations  orchestrated by the Bene Gesserit  sisterhood a secretive and powerful  order of women who manipulated the  inhabitants of the Imperium through use  of their many mysterious skills Paul is  a central character of the early novels  in dune mankind has spread out to more  than 10,000 worlds the Empire was  dominated by the landsraad which  consisted of many feuding noble houses  and was led by the padishah Emperor  himself 10,000 years prior to the start  of dune all thinking machines artificial  intelligence had been violently removed  from the Imperium during the but Larian  jihad such devices were forever banished  from this point on this at the time  destroyed mankind's ability to travel  safely at Lightspeed humanity moved on  in other ways however at the opening of  doom faster than life space travel is  possible due to the existence of Holzman  tribes  however for safe space travel to occur  precise predictive calculations are  required for this the guild navigators  undergo an accelerated process of  genetic mutations which misshapes them  but provides them with the ability to  predict and avoid obstacles in space  this would not be possible without the  use of spice for this reason the guild  maintains a monopoly on space travel  mélange often just called spice is the  most valued commodity in the Dune  universe it is a direct analog for oil  in the real  without spice no commerce would occur  between the thousands of worlds in the  Dune universe without spice the Empire  would fall spice also has properties  which allow it to greatly extend the  life of whoever consumes it without the  spice The Witches of the Bennett Jesuit  would lose many of their powers spice  increases longevity heightens awareness  and is also so addictive that if you  stop taking it the intense withdrawals  would mean your death there is no cure  for spice withdrawal symptoms spice is  found only on one planet in the Imperium  Arrakis also known as doom a harsh  desert planet where giant worms roam the  sands attacking all rhythmic motions  where the ancient Freeman descendants of  the Sun Sunni wander by night and still  suits which maintain the moisture of the  body in the desert water his life to  waste water would be unthinkable to a  Freeman  at the start of doom Paul Atreides and  his family moved to the planet Arrakis  they have been forced into a plot  orchestrated by the Emperor and also the  arch enemy of Paul's father Leto the  Baron Vladimir Harkonnen together the  Emperor and the harkonnens intend to  destroy the noble Atreides the original  doom novel details the awakening of  Paul's hidden abilities and his rise to  power over the next five novels Frank  Herbert teaches many things about the  trappings of power the nature and the  dangers of religious fanaticism and most  importantly the harm that can be caused  when individuals blindly follow their  leaders without question the doomed  series is an example of how an author  can completely subvert expectations but  in an interesting and clever way which  ultimately teaches us something about  the human condition with denis  villeneuve director of blade runner'  2049 and a rival currently working on  two major Hollywood productions based on  the first novel in the series there has  never been a better time to get into  dune Denis Villeneuve also seems  extremely passionate about the project  and has assembled a team of dedicated  and competent people to bring this story  to life on the big screen dune is  definitely a commitment to read so I  recommend to those of you who are  interested in getting into dune but  haven't yet to check out my ultimate  guide to doom series 